#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 356 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Routes the incoming audio signal to one of several audio
outputs \, according to the value on the control inlet. The number
of outputs is set by the argument N (or by the @n property). Only one
output at a time receives the signal — the others output zero. The
gain for each output can be set individually with the @value property.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Switching a single source between several effect
chains — routing one oscillator \, sample or voice to a specific effect
(reverb \, delay \, distortion) selected by a control signal.;
#X text 250 279 • Routing to different speakers or zones — sending
the same audio signal to one of several loudspeaker outputs \, for
example in an installation with multiple independent playback zones.;
#X text 250 349 • Selecting a destination in a matrix — choosing which
input of a multi-channel processor receives the signal \, by switching
the demultiplexer from a sequencer or a control UI.;
